WEBVTT

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.190
Sakunoshin, when am I leaving?

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:13.900
9 o'clock departure, miss.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.870
I am told that the master
will be arriving there directly.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.520
The afternoon inspection
would have been enough.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.240
I am no mere decoration for my father.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:29.330
Oh?

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:30.960
Yui-san.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.050
It's an invitation from Kaori-san.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.260
Call it an extracurricular activity
on your day off.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:17.490
So sleepy...

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:21.700
Sheesh. Are there any mornings that you're <i>not</i> sleepy, Prez?

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.600
How many hours did you get last night?

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:25.880
Three, I guess?

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:31.250
Jennifer would always say that lack of sleep
is the archenemy of beauty.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:34.340
Oh, my dear Jennifer!

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.200
That silky skin of yours!

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.260
I wanna touch you!

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:39.840
Thanks for the advice.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.020
Oh, this is it.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:41.760
Huh?

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:42.800
R-Right.

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:45.470
Okay, I'm off.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:48.770
But Airi-chan and the others
will be here soon.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:52.110
Some bigwigs are coming
for an inspection today.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:55.750
Welcome, Airi-chan.

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:59.130
Oh, Shiori-san, it's been a while.

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:00.360
Are you headed out?

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:03.600
I am. I need to pull some overtime.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.620
Um, are you Kenny-kun?

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:07.090
Y-Yes!

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:08.980
Who is it?

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.420
Shiori-san. Kaori's mother.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:13.920
Really?! Not her sister?

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:17.920
Welcome, Airi-chan, Kenny-kun.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:21.030
I'm sorry about this.
It's not every day that you come to visit.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:23.300
Oh, not at all. Please don't worry about it.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:26.050
Well, make yourselves at home.

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:27.890
Take care.
See you later.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:29.990
Hey, you made it.

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:31.560
Yo, Sou.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.310
Shall we begin?

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:35.830
Here. I bought these.

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:37.820
Milk, eggs, and butter.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:39.320
Right, thank you.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.560
That's all you need?

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:44.280
Yeah. I got the rest ready.

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:46.530
Sweets for the school festival, huh?

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:48.290
What kind of sweets are you going to make?

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:52.760
We have to make everything the day before,

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:55.220
so it'll be simple baked sweets and stuff,

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:57.410
but as long as we're doing this,
I'd like to go sophisticated.

00:03:57.410 --> 00:03:58.550
Agreed.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:02.950
I think homemade sweets by Kaori-chan
will attract fans in droves no matter what they are.

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:05.760
Isn't the main attraction
supposed to be the planetarium?

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.050
The café's just something extra, right?

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.640
They're both main attractions.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:12.810
If we're going to serve sweets,
we might as well make them good, right?

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:14.960
That's true, but...

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:17.730
Can you even make sweets in the first place?

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:21.300
How rude! I may not look it,
but I'm pretty good with my hands, you know.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.600
I've just never tried this before.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:25.950
Make sure you listen closely
to what Kaori tells you.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:27.460
What's that supposed to mean?

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:29.730
Well, let's get cooking already.

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:30.700
Okay.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:34.370
But will you be okay
with that sprained wrist, Kaori?

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:35.540
Oh, yeah.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.290
It's fine as long as I don't
do anything too strenuous.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.030
Well, don't push yourself too hard.

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:42.360
Thank you.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.360
Oh yeah, Yui said she'd be coming later too.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:46.400
Furukawa will be?

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:47.050
Yeah.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:50.210
Apparently Nagisa-san has other plans, though.

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:52.560
Wow, sounds like things are gonna get lively.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:55.090
Will Yui-chan be able to find our place okay?

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:58.810
I emailed a map to Nagisa-san, just to be safe.

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:32.430
Do we really need to go to the trouble of making this ourselves?

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:35.890
An off-the-shelf unit would work
well enough for a planetarium, right?

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:37.360
Don't be stupid.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:39.960
By that logic, the sweets
could be store-bought too,

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:41.400
and there'd be no need for us at all.

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:43.430
Yeah, true.

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:45.540
But, like, I'm so tired!

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.650
It hasn't even been half an hour!

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:50.840
This kind of quiet work isn't my thing.

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:53.650
Well, I wasn't counting on getting help
to start with anyway.

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:56.250
What are you doing?

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:58.640
Treasure...

00:05:58.640 --> 00:05:59.240
found!

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:00.040
Oh! Wait...

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.750
It's all good, right, my friend?

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:12.350
Sou-kun. Kenny-kun.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.100
The first batch just came out of the oven,

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:16.900
so we'd like you to taste-test them.

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:18.200
Oh, Kaori!

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:19.680
I see! They're done?

00:06:20.490 --> 00:06:21.940
What are you doing?

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:22.790
Nothing!

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:23.360
Stretching!
Taking a break!

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:24.580
Oh...

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:28.170
Yui-chan.

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:29.610
Hello.

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:31.570
Scones!

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:32.870
These look good!

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:36.760
We just finished baking
test batch number one.

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:38.120
It smells good.

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:40.520
Yui-chan, you taste-test them too.

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:42.130
I'll go make some tea.

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:43.880
Did you walk here?

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:47.760
Yes. The weather was fine,
so it was good for photosynthesis as well.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.700
You mean suntanning, right?

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:51.220
So close!

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:55.180
If only Nagisa-san were here, we'd have the whole gang.

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:58.070
It seems Nagisa-san
will be coming later as well.

00:06:58.070 --> 00:06:59.140
She is?

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:00.560
It's good!

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:02.850
Hey! I didn't say you could
dig into them already!

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:05.360
Huh? Aren't we taste-testing?

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.360
What you're doing is just sneaking food!

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:08.240
No more for you!

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:09.360
No!

00:07:10.170 --> 00:07:12.770
It's okay. There's plenty more.

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:14.680
Kaori-chan, you're an angel.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:15.570
And what am I?

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:16.370
A demon.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:20.100
Here, Kenny-kun.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:21.660
Thanks!

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:22.370
What do you think?

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:26.500
It's good.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:27.860
It is delicious.

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:30.800
Excellent, if I do say so myself.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:33.440
Kaori did most of the work anyway, right?

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:36.510
I sifted the flour and used
the molds and stuff, too!

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:40.270
This'll be a must-get item
at the Astronomy Club.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:43.240
All right, this one definitely
goes on the menu,

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:45.730
but it'd be nice to have
a couple more items.

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:48.270
I'm thinking of trying to
bake some cookies next.

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:50.050
Sounds good.

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:51.780
Yui-chan, will you help too?

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:53.410
Oh, yes.

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:55.410
Okay, you're good.

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:58.390
Yui-chan, do you know how to cook?

00:07:58.390 --> 00:07:59.790
I...

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:01.890
Maybe she doesn't remember.

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:04.290
Oh, right. I'm sorry.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:05.550
Oh, no...

00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:07.790
Then I'll teach you.

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:09.550
Okay.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:15.050
You use the whisk like this.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:34.530
Are you going to make holes
for the constellations with that?

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:35.690
Yeah.

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:39.030
Subtly different-sized holes
reproduce the magnitude of the stars.

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:40.200
I have to be careful.

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:43.300
About how many holes
are you going to make?

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:44.710
Let me think...

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:48.460
They say that several thousand stars are visible to the naked eye, so...

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:51.430
Jesus! That's stupid.

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:52.210
Hey...

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:54.970
About how long until they're done?

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:57.600
About thirteen or fourteen minutes, I think?

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:59.720
Um, Sasaki-san.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:00.740
Hm?

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:03.300
Could I have a moment later?

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:05.800
There is something I want
to talk to you about.

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:06.450
What?

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:09.480
What's this? Something you can't talk about in front of me?

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:11.980
Oh, um...

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:15.460
Well, could it wait until this batch
is out of the oven?

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:18.240
What is it? Tell me.

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:20.950
Um, after that, then.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.190
What?

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:24.120
Woohoo!

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:27.920
This model's butt is shaped just like Jennifer's!

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:29.070
Oh!

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:29.880
What's wrong, Sou?

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:33.280
Shoot. I made Shaula too big.

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:37.590
It just has to be in the general ballpark, right?
No one'll care whether it's exact.

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:40.880
No. What if someone unusually well-versed in the stars happens to...

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:42.510
Jennifer...

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:45.590
If only I had some better tools.

00:09:45.590 --> 00:09:46.950
I want to reproduce the colors, too.

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:48.520
Jennifer...

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:53.480
Yup. These are done just right.

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:54.940
They be smellin' mighty fine.

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:57.170
Looks-wise, it's another story.

00:09:57.170 --> 00:09:58.950
Well, they're the first batch, after all.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.880
Mm, delicious!

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.150
Oh? Where's Yui-chan?

00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:10.420
No idea. Bathroom, maybe?

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:29.020
I will be sure to return it to you later.

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:32.980
Oh, Yui-chan.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.940
The cookies are done. Try one.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:41.950
It's good.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:43.340
I'm glad.

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:45.910
Hey, Yui-chan said they're good, too.

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:48.680
I think I'll have another one.

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:50.420
I'm glad they turned out well.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:51.280
No kidding.

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:02.470
I'm done over here.

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:03.220
Thanks.

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:07.870
As for this, I guess I'll just have to do it myself.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:12.450
Test batch number two is done.

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:15.520
Woohoo! I've been waiting for this!

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:19.680
The shapes are kind of all over the place.

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:22.210
I told you they're a test batch, didn't I? Here.

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:23.280
R-Right.

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:26.090
How are things on your end?

00:11:26.090 --> 00:11:27.960
I think we can finish most of it today.

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:29.620
Hey, don't step there.

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:30.720
Whoops!

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:31.440
Your room is as boring as ever, I see.

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:32.770
Delicious!

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:33.170
Your room is as boring as ever, I see.

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:35.080
You try one too.

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:36.240
Later.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:37.810
Sheesh. Here.

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:41.930
It's good.

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:43.180
Right?

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:45.000
Let's see...

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:46.120
Got it.

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:49.890
Sasaki-san, do you have feelings for Akiyama-san?

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:52.940
Wh-Why are you asking me that all of a sudden?

00:11:53.550 --> 00:11:55.440
If things stay like this, and the future...

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:58.260
If this life were to continue on,

00:11:58.260 --> 00:12:00.570
I wonder what would become of you two.

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:02.640
Wh-Who knows.

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:05.390
Sou-kun and I are just childhood friends, after all.

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:07.830
Yui-chan?

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:11.280
Yui-chan, could it be that...

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:12.160
Sasaki-san.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:13.460
Wh-What?

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:17.110
We were close to running out of tea
in the club room, as I recall.

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:18.800
We will need to resupply.

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:22.370
O-Oh, that's right.
You have a good memory.

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:23.730
Kaori!

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:26.050
Oh, Airi-chan's back.

00:12:26.420 --> 00:12:28.470
Sou says he's going on a supply run.

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:29.640
A supply run?

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:32.430
Yeah, there are a couple things I want to get.

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:35.280
I thought I'd pop out to the shops.

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:37.190
Then let's all go together.

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:39.190
Let's go!

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:42.440
I want to try making more
different kinds of sweets, too,

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:44.420
so I need to buy ingredients.

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:50.480
If you'd told me what you needed,
I could've just bought them for you.

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:52.870
But it's fun to go shopping
with everyone, isn't it?

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:00.760
We'll be going to the underground grocery section.

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:02.630
We're looking for miscellaneous supplies, so...

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:03.790
Upstairs, I guess?

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:06.220
Uh... Oh, wait.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:09.670
Kenny-kun, would you help us with our stuff?

00:13:09.670 --> 00:13:12.230
I still can't carry heavy things with my wrist.

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:13.220
Okey!

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:15.870
What is it that you need to buy so much of?

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:18.980
Well, all kinds of things.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.490
In exchange, Yui-chan,
you take care of things with Sou-kun.

00:13:21.490 --> 00:13:22.150
What?

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:25.160
Keep an eye on him
and make sure he doesn't waste money.

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:26.150
What am I, a child?

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:30.770
Um, Sasaki-san, do not forget the tea I mentioned earlier...

00:13:30.770 --> 00:13:32.160
I know.

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:38.320
Why did you put those two together?

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:40.760
What? No real reason, I guess.

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:45.380
Is that the tea you like that we always have in our club room?

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:49.120
Yeah, we were close to running out.

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:50.800
If Yui-chan hadn't mentioned it,

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:52.890
I would've had to come out again to get it.

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:54.420
I see.

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:57.830
Okay, I think that's everything.

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:00.150
Huh? Where's Furukawa?

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:06.780
There she is.

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:14.040
This kind of looks like the one Kaori has.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:16.750
Furukawa, sorry to keep you waiting.

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:18.710
Sorry to drag you along.

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.280
Did you find something interesting?

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:22.630
No, I did not.

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:24.140
Oh, okay.

00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:27.970
Hey.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:32.470
Want me to carry that?

00:14:33.050 --> 00:14:35.220
Yeah, thank you.

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:38.400
Sou, that looks good.

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:39.800
Mind letting me have a bite?

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:41.690
Order your own.

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:43.410
No money...

00:14:43.410 --> 00:14:45.160
Then build a bridge and get over it.

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:46.690
You can have one of mine.

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:49.140
Oh, Prez!

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:49.560
Thanks so very, very, very much!

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:51.330
It's fun when we're all together, isn't it?

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:51.750
Okay, okay already.

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:52.700
Yes.

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:56.950
What are we making next?

00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:59.920
I think we'll try baking a pound cake.

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:02.370
Sounds good! Great idea!

00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:04.340
What are you doing here?

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:06.680
The work I was given is done.

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:08.710
So I'll take care of the taste-testing from now on.

00:15:08.710 --> 00:15:10.400
Just how hungry are you?

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:12.070
I'm still growing, you know!

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:12.510
Oh, you can't have these!

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:13.220
Um...

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:17.850
Then I will go help Akiyama-san.

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:20.320
You can go, but there won't
be anything for you to do.

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:21.850
No, you go, Yui-chan.

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:29.530
Okay. That's looking good.

00:15:30.170 --> 00:15:30.780
Oh...

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:32.550
Furukawa.

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:34.990
I thought I might be able to help in some way.

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:40.000
You really love the stars, don't you?

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:41.090
Yeah.

00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:42.640
Why is that?

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:44.750
I'm not so sure myself.

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:51.170
When I saw the stars as a kid, they were really beautiful and I remember being in awe, but...

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:54.720
Have you heard?

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:59.970
The starlight that we see from the
Earth's surface is really ancient light.

00:15:59.970 --> 00:16:03.110
It comes from far across space,
taking a long, long time to get here.

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:05.270
It's light that's reached
the end of a great journey.

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:10.450
The distance between the Andromeda Galaxy and Earth is 2.39 million light-years.

00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:14.380
What we're seeing is 2.39 million-year-old light.

00:16:14.970 --> 00:16:19.260
I can't even begin to imagine time or distance on the order of 2.39 million years.

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:24.190
Try shining this light through from inside.

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:38.360
How about that?

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:41.300
I haven't put in the colors yet, though.

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:46.850
These are the constellations
of summer, aren't they?

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:47.810
You can tell?

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:49.260
Yes.

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:17.340
Come to think of it, Furukawa,

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:20.240
have you remembered anything since then?

00:17:22.720 --> 00:17:25.250
Well, not that there's any rush.

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:27.260
I'm sure you will eventually.

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:28.610
A face in profile...

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:33.440
A certain person's face in profile...
I remember that.

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:39.490
They're smiling, but at the same time,
they seem very sad.

00:17:43.390 --> 00:17:45.780
Is that person someone
close to you or something?

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:48.720
Is it... someone close to me?

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:50.270
I don't know...

00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:54.740
But it must be someone you have a deep connection with.

00:17:54.740 --> 00:17:56.340
Why do you say that?

00:17:56.340 --> 00:18:00.600
Because you looked sad
talking about it just now, too.

00:18:01.690 --> 00:18:03.880
That may be true.

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:04.850
I think they must be...

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:09.870
someone very precious to me.

00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:11.140
I see.

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:20.910
Okay, first, second,
and third magnitude stars are all done!

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:25.920
Furukawa. Furukawa.

00:18:31.150 --> 00:18:32.150
Sou.

00:18:32.150 --> 00:18:33.190
What?

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:34.690
I am Yui.

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:37.140
Please call me Yui.

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:38.290
Like you always do.

00:18:38.290 --> 00:18:41.010
Wait... A-Are you still half-asleep?

00:18:41.900 --> 00:18:43.380
I...

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:51.190
A-Anyway, once we do a rough assembly,
want to go see how the others are doing? Yui...

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:53.190
Okay.

00:18:55.050 --> 00:18:55.690
What the?

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:58.690
Huh? Did Kaori come by?

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:01.640
Tasty! It's good!

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:04.210
That's all you've been saying.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:06.550
Yeah, it <i>is</i> good.

00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:07.200
Yes!

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:11.600
So... which should we do in the end?

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:12.800
Hmm...

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:15.200
Like them all!

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:16.710
I like everything!

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:18.160
That's an option too.

00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:19.970
But that'll be a lot of work.

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:22.740
And that's why we'll be counting on you!

00:19:22.740 --> 00:19:24.470
Airi-chan...

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:28.660
When you get down to it, you really think some planetarium's gonna get customers in the door?

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:33.410
Ultimately, we've got it all riding on
your cosplay and homemade sweets.

00:19:33.410 --> 00:19:37.800
I'm not sure that's something you should be saying as president of the Astronomy Club.

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:38.550
Oh?

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:41.490
I guess even you can be the voice of reason every once in a while, Kenny-san.

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:43.240
Nagisa-san!

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:46.360
Wow, that's Kaori-san for you.

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:48.070
They all look so good.

00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:51.250
Um, I helped out too, you know...

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:53.730
Please taste-test them as well, Hanamiya-senpai.

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:55.920
Oh, it's Senpai.

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:57.040
Well, then...

00:19:57.040 --> 00:19:58.300
Yo.

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:00.480
You done with whatever you were doing?

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:04.050
Yes. I'm sorry that I wasn't able to be of any use.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:07.300
For some reason, it's scary
hearing that from Nagisa-kun.

00:20:07.300 --> 00:20:09.990
Well, I had to come pick up Yui-san anyway.

00:20:09.990 --> 00:20:11.520
You came at the perfect time.

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:14.310
It's still not finalized,
but we've built the planetarium.

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:16.810
Wow, so this is it!

00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:18.730
Okay, I'm turning out the lights.

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:23.580
Whoa!

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:26.820
Fantastic!

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:29.810
Wow, this is amazing.

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:31.330
You made this, Sou-san?

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:36.710
Well, Kenny built the base,
and Yui helped out toward the end too.

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:40.230
Yui? Why are you suddenly
on a first-name basis?

00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:42.840
I-It doesn't really matter, does it?

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:44.590
Now I'm suspicious.

00:20:44.940 --> 00:20:47.440
N-Never mind that. Look at the stars!

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:51.040
Uh, look, right around there
is the Summer Triangle.

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:53.300
The star nerd's in his element, I see.

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:56.100
Vega in the Summer Triangle looks whitish,

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:58.900
but Antares of Scorpius in
the southern skies of summer

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:02.900
is called a red supergiant
after the light it gives off.

00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:06.120
As for why there are these various colors,

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:07.890
it's caused by different surface temperatures.

00:21:07.890 --> 00:21:10.280
The red Antares is roughly 3,500 degrees,

00:21:10.280 --> 00:21:12.410
while the white Vega is 9,500 degrees.

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:16.110
Incidentally, our sun's surface temperature is about 6,000 degrees, and...

00:21:16.640 --> 00:21:17.220
Yui?

00:21:18.260 --> 00:21:19.650
Oh, yes?

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:20.530
What's wrong?

00:21:20.530 --> 00:21:22.500
No, nothing...

00:21:22.500 --> 00:21:23.550
Uh, okay.

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:28.110
Thanks for your help today.

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:31.430
I've still only gotten up to the third magnitude stars,

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:33.720
but it looks like we'll manage by the school festival.

00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:36.480
I had fun too.

00:21:37.030 --> 00:21:39.060
Y-Yeah?

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:41.730
Well, the hard part's still to come, though.

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:45.740
Once we add the even-smaller fourth and fifth magnitude stars, we'll have close to 3,000 holes.

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:48.580
The magnitude is determined by brightness,

00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:51.490
but there's the actual brightness and the observed brightness,

00:21:51.490 --> 00:21:54.260
which are called absolute magnitude and apparent magnitude, but...

00:21:54.260 --> 00:21:55.960
This planetarium uses the apparent magnitude, more or less.

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:28.160
She's been weird since this morning.

00:23:28.160 --> 00:23:29.410
Did you touch her boobs?!

00:23:29.410 --> 00:23:30.200
What are you doing?

00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:31.320
You seem so panicked.

00:23:31.320 --> 00:23:32.160
Ten more minutes...

00:23:32.160 --> 00:23:33.030
Kaori's not around?

00:23:33.030 --> 00:23:34.100
You can't come this way!

00:23:34.600 --> 00:23:35.820
See you again tomorrow.

00:23:36.360 --> 00:23:40.140
Episode eight: "Shooting Stars Passing in the Night."
